ATTRIBUTION

If you use this benchmark, please cite:

    Lisa Bylinina. 2026. Augustinian BabyLM: What Ostensive Definition Can
    and Cannot Teach a Small Language Model. In Proceedings of the BabyLM
    Workshop.

and the upstream protocol it follows:

    Dongyan Lin et al. 2026. EgoBabyVLM: Benchmarking Cross-Modal Learning
    from Naturalistic Egocentric Video Data. arXiv:2605.19130.


RELATION TO UPSTREAM

The task design follows the Visual-Property Swap protocol of EgoBabyVLM
(facebookresearch/egobabyvlm, apps/swapbench/visual_property_swap), which is
released under CC BY-NC 4.0. The items distributed here were generated
independently: they are built from the bb24.train corpus rather than an
external word list, use different generator and judge models, and add
per-item seeded-status metadata absent upstream. The construction code in
this repository is an independent implementation of the described protocol,
not a copy or adaptation of the upstream source. Deviations are documented
in README.md.

Anyone reusing this benchmark should consult the upstream license for their
own use of EgoBabyVLM materials.


CAVEAT

Items are generated by an LLM generator and filtered by an LLM judge, and
therefore reflect those models' notions of typical object properties, which
may encode cultural or distributional biases. This benchmark is a diagnostic
probe, not a source of ground-truth world knowledge.
